hadiths[44]{hadithnumber,text}:
"838","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""The Prophets (peace be upon them) are paternal brothers; their mothers are different. I am the most deserving of ‘Isa ibn Maryam (peace be upon him), because there is no prophet between me and him. He will descend, so recognize him: he will be of medium height and of a reddish-white complexion, drops will be falling from his head even though water has not touched it. He will break the cross, kill the pig, take possession of wealth and abolish the jizya. Allah will destroy all religions except Islam during his time. Allah will destroy the one-eyed false messiah. Allah will fill the earth with peace so that lions will graze with camels, leopards with cows, and wolves with sheep; children will play with snakes, and they will not harm one another."""
"839","Qatadah narrated from a man, from the chain of Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), a narration similar to this, but he narrated somewhat less than it."
"840","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Those who rule will wish that they had fallen from Thurayya (the Pleiades) rather than having accepted anything from this rulership."" Marwan said: Please elaborate further. He (Abu Hurairah) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""The destruction of this Ummah will be at the hands of a few young men from the Quraysh."""
"841","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""A time is near when a trial will appear, none will be saved except Allah, or the one who supplicates with a supplication like that of a drowning person."""
"842","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""A time will come upon the people when a man will be given a choice between incapacity and wickedness."""
"843","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: There is no punishment upon this Ummah; its punishment is in its own hands. It was asked of him, ""How can its punishment be in its own hands?"" He replied: ""Was not the Battle of Siffin a punishment? Was not the Battle of Nahrawan a punishment? Was not the Battle of Jamal a punishment?"" The narrator stated: I said to Abu Dawud (may Allah have mercy on him): Who narrated it from Sa'd? He said: Yahya bin Abi Zaidah did."
"844","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""The Hour will not be established until you fight against people whose shoes will be made of hair, and you will fight against people whose faces will be broad and noses flat, as if their faces are like layered shields."""
"845","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Near the Day of Judgment, you will fight against a people whose shoes will be made of hair; you will fight against a people whose faces will be flat, their eyes small, as if their faces are like folded shields. By the One in whose hand is the life of Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)! If any one of you were to carry a bundle of wood on his back, sell it, become self-sufficient through it, give charity from it, and eat from it, that would be better for him than going to someone and asking him, whether he gives or withholds. The upper hand is better than the lower hand, and begin spending on those under your care. The smell from the mouth of a fasting person is better with Allah than the fragrance of musk."""
"846","Qais bin Abu Hazim narrated: When Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) came with Sayyiduna Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him), we presented ourselves before them. So we went to them, and they said to him: These people have come to you so that you may narrate to them a hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). So he mentioned a narration similar to the previous one, and he stated: ""Those with red faces, small eyes."" And he said: ""The smell from the mouth of the fasting person."""
"847","Asim bin Kulayb narrated: My father told me that I was sitting with Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) in the mosque of Kufa, when a man came to him and said: ""You say that you will pray with ‘Isa ibn Maryam (peace be upon him)?"" He replied: ""O people of Iraq! I knew that you would not think well of me, but this does not prevent me from telling you what the truthful and trusted Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) told us: 'The Dajjal will appear from the east among a group of people and will travel everywhere in forty days. He will make every effort to overpower the believers. In that era, the believers will suffer from famine. Then ‘Isa ibn Maryam (peace be upon him) will descend and he will lead them in prayer. When he raises his head from bowing, Allah Almighty will destroy the Dajjal and his companions.' As for my saying that it is true, it is because the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'It is true.' As for my saying: I hope that I will reach that time, it may be that I do reach it. You see the whiteness in my hair, the weakness in my body, and my old age. May Allah have mercy on me, if I reach them and pray with him (‘Isa, peace be upon him). Go back to your people and tell them what Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) has told you about this."" The man asked: ""Where will this be?"" So he picked up some pebbles from the mosque and said: ""From here."" The man repeated the question, so he said: ""Do you want me to say from the mosque of Kufa? He will emerge from the earth, before it is changed (i.e., before the Day of Resurrection), and Allah will make it wherever He wills."""
"848","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""The trustworthy will be accused (of betrayal), the untrustworthy will be called trustworthy, the liar will be considered truthful and the truthful will be considered a liar, and «شرف جور» will descend upon you."" They asked: O Messenger of Allah! What is meant by «شرف جور» ? He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Trials (fitan) will descend like pieces of a dark night."""
"849","Musa bin Ali narrated from his father, he said: I set out for Hajj, so Salim bin 'Itr, who was the judge of the people of Egypt during the rule of 'Amr bin al-'As (may Allah be pleased with him) and after him, advised me to convey his greetings to Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), and he said: Yesterday I prayed for forgiveness for his father and mother. So when I met Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) in Madinah, I conveyed the greetings to him, and he said: Yesterday I prayed for forgiveness for him and his family. Then he said: How did you leave Umm Khunur (Egypt)? Tell us about its condition. He said: The first corruption will arise in that land, then after that in Armenia. He narrated: I said to him: Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)? He said: Then who else, Ka'b the one with two books?"
"850","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: A wolf came to a shepherd of sheep and seized a sheep from the flock. The shepherd chased after it and rescued the sheep from it. The wolf sat on a mound and said: I intended a provision/sustenance that Allah had granted me, but you snatched it away from me. The man said: By Allah! I have never seen a wolf speak like today. The wolf said: Is it not more astonishing that there is a man between two rocky fields, among the palm groves, who tells you about past and future events? The narrator said: That man was a Jew. He came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and informed him, then accepted Islam. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) affirmed it and said: “This is one of the signs before the occurrence of the Hour. It is near that a man will leave his house and when he returns, his shoes will inform him of what happened, and his whip will tell him what his family did after him.”"
"851","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates in a marfu’ form that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “The destruction and ruin of this Ummah will be at the hands of young, foolish boys from the Quraysh.”"
"852","With this same chain, the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Hasten to perform good deeds before six things occur: the emergence of the beast, the rising of the sun from the west, the coming of the Dajjal, the appearance of the smoke, before death comes, and before the appearance of tribulations."""
"853","It is narrated with the same chain that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The Hour will be established upon the worst of people."""
"854","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""Allah has protected you from three things: that you will not all gather upon misguidance, that the people of falsehood will not prevail over the people of truth, and that I have prayed for you that He does not destroy you, and in exchange for them He has given you three things: smoke, the Dajjal, and the Beast of the Earth (the creature that will emerge from the earth)."""
"855","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""The Hour will not be established until you see a thrown shoe, and a man will say: It is as if it is a Qurayshi shoe."""
"856","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""The Hour will not be established until about thirty women pursue one man, all of them saying: Marry me, marry me, marry me."""
"857","With this same chain, it is narrated from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, that he said: ""Before the Day of Resurrection, there will be tribulations like pieces of a dark night. In those tribulations, a man will be a believer in the morning and a disbeliever in the evening, and if he is a believer in the evening, he will be a disbeliever in the morning. In them, people will sell their religion for a small portion of worldly goods and possessions."""
"858","With this same chain, it is narrated from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, that he said: ""There are only two elevations: the elevation of good and the elevation of evil. So let not the elevation of evil be more beloved to any of you than the elevation of good."""
"859","With this chain of narration, the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Allah has granted you protection from three things: that all of you will not unite upon misguidance, falsehood will not prevail over you, and you will not make such a supplication that all of you are destroyed. However, for you, the Dajjal, the smoke, and the beast of the earth are inevitable."""
"860","Narrated with the same chain, the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""The source/head of disbelief is from the direction of the East."""
"861","And with this, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, he said: ""There will not cease to be a group from my Ummah striving in the way of Allah; those who oppose them will not harm them until the command of Allah comes while they are manifest."""
"862","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""By Him in Whose hand is my soul! The world will not end until a man passes by a grave and says: 'Would that this were my grave!' He will not say this because of religion, but only because of (worldly) hardships."""
"863","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""The Beast of the Earth will emerge, with it will be the staff of Musa (peace be upon him) and the ring of Sulaiman (peace be upon him). With the staff, the face of the believer will be illuminated, and with the ring, the nose of the disbeliever will be sealed. People will gather at the dining spread, and it (the Beast) will say: This is a believer, and it will say: This is a disbeliever."""
"864","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""Five things will appear, which of these signs will occur first, at that time the faith of any soul will not benefit it if it had not believed before: (these signs are) the rising of the sun from the west, the Dajjal, Gog and Magog, the smoke, and the appearance of the beast."""
"865","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Today, a hole has been made in the barrier of Gog and Magog like this."" The narrator, Mumil, made a circle of ten with his hand."
"866","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: I know about a forthcoming tribulation, but I do not know the way out of it. He was asked: What is the way out of it? He replied: That I be held with my hand in this manner until a man comes to me and kills me."
"867","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) mentioned India one day and said: ""A group of your army will attack India, and Allah will grant them victory, until they bring the kings of Sindh in chains. Allah will forgive their sins. When they return, they will find Isa ibn Maryam (Jesus, son of Mary) in Syria."" Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) said: If I live to see that campaign, I will sell my mount and my property and participate in that campaign. When Allah grants us victory and we return, I will be Abu Huraira, freed from Hell, returning to Syria. He (i.e., Isa ibn Maryam, peace be upon him) will meet them, so I will strive very hard to be close to him and to inform him that I have been with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). The narrator said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) smiled and said: ""His second coming will not be like the first coming. He will cast an awe like that of death. He will wipe the faces of the dead and inform them about the ranks of Paradise."""
"868","Narrated from Sayyida Asma bint Yazid (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was present in her house and Asma (may Allah be pleased with her) was kneading dough, when they mentioned the Dajjal. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""One year before his emergence, a third of the rain will be withheld from the sky, and the earth will not produce a third of its vegetation. In the second year, the sky will withhold two-thirds of its rain, and the earth will not produce two-thirds of its vegetation. And in the third year, the sky will withhold all its rain, and the earth will not produce any kind of vegetation, until there will not remain any cattle, etc. The greatest trial will be that he will say to a man: 'Tell me, if I bring your father or your brother back to life for you, will you then know that I am your Lord?' He will say: 'Yes.' He will say to a Bedouin: 'Tell me, if I bring your camel back to life for you, with a hump longer than before and udders larger than before, will you then know that I am your Lord?' He will say: 'Yes.' Then he will make the devils appear in their forms, while he cannot actually bring the dead to life."" Then the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) went outside for some task, and when he returned, his noble Companions (may Allah be pleased with them) were weeping. The Prophet (peace be upon him) held the door frame and said: ""Be silent."" Sayyida Asma (may Allah be pleased with her) said: O Messenger of Allah! The mention of the Dajjal has been made to them, which has been hard on them. By Allah! We are anxious while you are among us; what will our state be when you are not with us? The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""If he (the Dajjal) emerges while I am among you, I will argue and debate with him on your behalf. And if he emerges after me, then Allah is my successor over every believer."" Sayyida Asma (may Allah be pleased with her) said: O Messenger of Allah! What will suffice for people in terms of food on that day? The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""That which suffices the inhabitants of the heavens in glorification and sanctification."""
"869","Lady Asma (may Allah be pleased with her), daughter of Yazid Al-Ansariyyah (may Allah be pleased with her), narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came to my house while I was kneading dough. He (peace be upon him) said: ""Before the Dajjal, there will be three years; in the first year, the sky will withhold a third of its rain, and the earth will withhold a third of its vegetation."" Then he narrated similar to the previous hadith, and regarding the camels, he said: ""The devils will take on forms for them like their camels, even better than their previous state, and their udders will be much larger than before,"" and he said: ""He will take on the form of fathers and sons (children),"" and he said: ""All cows and camels will perish."" Lady Asma (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: I said, O Messenger of Allah! We knead dough but do not bake bread until we feel hungry; what will be the condition of the believers on that day? He (peace be upon him) said: ""That which suffices the inhabitants of the heavens in glorification and sanctification will suffice them."""
"870","Narrated from Sayyida Asma bint Yazid Ash’ariyyah (may Allah be pleased with her), she heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) saying while he was among his companions: “I warn and caution you against the Messiah Dajjal, and every prophet has warned his people about him. O Ummah! He will be among you. I am describing him to you in such a clear manner that no prophet has described him like this before. There will be five years of famine before his emergence, until all livestock will perish in them.” A man called out to him and asked: O Messenger of Allah! What will suffice the believers for food on that day? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “That which suffices the angels will suffice them. Then he (Dajjal) will emerge while he is one-eyed, and Allah is not one-eyed. ‘Kafir’ (disbeliever) will be written on his forehead, and every literate and illiterate person will read it. Most of his followers will be Jews, Bedouins, and women. You will see rain falling from the sky, but he will not send rain. You will see the earth producing vegetation, but it will not produce. He will say to the Bedouins: What do you want from me? Did I not send down heavy rain for you? Did I not revive your livestock for you, which are fat, their bellies protruding, and their udders full of milk?” He said: “Satan will appear to them in the images of their fathers, brothers, and friends. So a man will come to his father, his brother, or his relative, and he will say to him: Are you not so-and-so? Do you not affirm me? He is your Lord, so follow him. He (Dajjal) will remain for forty years: a year like a month, a month like a week, a week like a day, and a day like a spark in the fire. He will go to every pass except the two mosques (Makkah and Madinah).” Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) stood up to perform ablution, and he heard the weeping and wailing of his noble companions (may Allah be pleased with them all), so he returned and said: “Rejoice! If he appears while I am among you, then Allah and His Messenger are sufficient for you. And if he appears after me, then Allah is my successor among you.”"
"871","Sayyida Asma bint Yazid (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""The Dajjal will remain on the earth for forty years; a year will be like a month, a month like a week, a week like a day, and a day will be like a flame in the fire."""
"872","Umm Malik al-Bahziyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) mentioned tribulations, and said: ""The best among you during those tribulations is the one who takes his wealth and withdraws, worships his Lord, and fulfills His due. And another is the one whom the enemy does not know and he does not know them."""
"873","Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came to me, and I recognized that something had prompted him to hurry. He did not speak to anyone, but performed ablution and went out. I heard him from among the rooms saying: ""Allah says: O people! Enjoin good and forbid evil before a time comes when you pray to Allah and He does not accept your prayers, you ask Him and He does not grant you, and you seek His help and He does not help you."""
"874","Sayyida Fatimah bint Qays (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""Every prophet has warned (his nation) about the trial of Dajjal. O Ummah! He will appear among you, but he will roam the entire earth except for Taybah (Madina Munawwara)."""
"875","Lady Fatimah bint Qais (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) once sat on the pulpit, smiling, and said: ""Tamim al-Dari (may Allah be pleased with him) has told me something which has made me happy, so I liked to tell you as well, so that you may also be pleased with what your Prophet is pleased with. He told me that some people from Palestine boarded a ship in the sea, and it carried them to one of the sea islands and landed them there. There, they saw an animal whose clothing was made of hair. They said: 'Who are you?' It said: 'I am Jassasah.' They said: 'Tell us about something.' It said: 'I will not tell you anything nor ask you anything, but go to the farthest edge of this settlement, there is someone there who will tell you and ask you.' We reached the farthest edge of the settlement and there was a man bound in chains. He said: 'Tell me about the spring of Zughar.' We said: 'It is full and gushing.' He said: 'Tell me about the Lake of Tiberias.' We said: 'It is full and gushing.' He said: 'Tell me about the date palms of Baisan, which is between Palestine and Jordan, are they bearing fruit?' We said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Tell me about this unlettered Arab Prophet, has he appeared among you?' We said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Are people entering Islam?' We said: 'Rapidly.' He jumped so forcefully that he was about to break his chains. We said: 'Who are you?' He said: 'I am the Dajjal. He will enter all cities except Tayyibah.'"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This is Tayyibah."" He said it three times, meaning Madinah Munawwarah."
"876","Lady Fatimah bint Qais (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came one day at noon, and this was a time when he would not usually come. He sat on the pulpit and said: ""O people! I have not stood here at this time to give you any encouragement or warning, but Tamim Dari came to me and told me such news that, out of happiness and coolness of my eyes, I could not even take my midday nap. I wanted to convey to you the happiness of your Prophet. He came to me and told me that some of his cousins undertook a sea journey, a storm overtook them, and brought them to an unknown island. They traveled in small boats and reached the shore. There, they saw a creature with large eyelashes, thick hair, and dark skin. They did not know whether it was a man or a woman. They said to it: Who are you? It said: I am Jassasah. They said to it: Will you not tell us about something? It said: I will neither tell you about anything nor ask you, but in that temple near which you are, there is someone who is eager to tell you something and ask you something (so go there). They went to the temple and saw there a being who was tightly bound. He appeared very distressed and was sighing deeply. They greeted him, and he replied to their greeting. Then he said to them: Where are you from? We said: From Syria. He said: What is the condition of the Arabs? Has their Prophet appeared? They said: Yes. He said: What is his condition? Did his people oppose him, and Allah granted him victory over them? They said: Yes. He said: Are the Arabs now in such a state that their God is one, and their word is one? They said: Yes. He said: That is better for them. He said: What is the condition of the date orchards between Oman and Baisan? They said: They are fine and bear fruit every year. He said: What is the condition of the spring of Zughar? They said: It is fine; the people there drink from it themselves and irrigate their fields and orchards from it. He said: What is the condition of the Lake of Tiberias? They said: It is full, overflowing from both banks due to the abundance of water. He sighed deeply, then swore and said: If I am released from this captivity, I will trample the whole earth under my feet. Then he sighed deeply and said: Except for Taybah (Madina Munawwarah), I will have no power over it."" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hearing this, my happiness knew no bounds. This is Taybah. By the One in whose hand is my soul! This is Taybah. Allah has made my sanctuary forbidden to the Dajjal."" Then he (peace and blessings be upon him) swore: ""Until the Day of Resurrection, an angel with a drawn sword will stand guard; the Dajjal cannot enter it."""
"877","Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: ""Two sanctuaries: Makkah and Madinah are forbidden to him (the Dajjal)."""
"878","Shu’bi (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated: I met Al-Muharrar bin Abi Hurairah, so I narrated to him the narration of Fatimah bint Qais (may Allah be pleased with her). He said: I was with my father when he narrated this hadith to me exactly as Fatimah bint Qais (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated it to you; he did not omit a single letter from it. My father added one chapter to it; he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) drew a line with his hand towards the east about twenty times."
"879","Abu Asamah said: The person who heard from Amir narrated the hadith to me, he transmitted an addition in the hadith, that they asked him: Did people later prepare a reward, and in it is that he struck his foot with the inner part of his foot, and in it is that he said: Is it from the direction of Yemen, then he said: No, rather from the direction of Al-'Inan."
"880","Sayyidah Salamah bint al-Hurr (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""A time will come upon the people when they will stand for a period, but they will not find any imam to lead them in prayer."""
"881","Abdur Razzaq bin Hammam bin Nafi’ al-San’ani narrated: I heard my father narrating from some scholars, they said: The iqamah for prayer will be called, and people will push one another forward for leading the prayer. So this one will say to that one: Go ahead, and that one will say to this one: Go ahead, until they are swallowed up by the earth."
